Z||000000||85seNUT||01-24-2001||09:15 PM||||Hey i was wondering how hard it is to put in white face guages.  cuz i found some for around 25 dollars and i was wondering how long or how difficult it would be to put them in myself.||||reg||5
Z||000001||ferg||01-25-2001||04:29 PM||||I've never installed the gauges in a fiero, but I did it to my GMC pickup. In my pickup I used APC white face gauges-blue numbers. This kit is a sticker- <P>The biggest problem I had was getting all the needles to be in the right spot- I never got it totally correct, so I had to compensate and guess at it. <P>I've never taken the gauges out of my fiero so I don't know how hard it is- but I'm guessing that it's fairly simple.<P>If anyone know how put the needles in the right spot let me know.<P>BTW- White face gauges look AWESOME at night- in my truck the center of the guages looked like an eclipse, very cool looking- sorry no pics of the guages.||||reg||1
Z||000002||TheFiero64||01-25-2001||05:17 PM||||Was not too bad. It is basically stickers that just stick over the black.<P>here is mine done.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dashj.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||4
Z||000003||sqoach||01-25-2001||05:21 PM||||just a little bit o/t<P>are there any for a 85 speedo?<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||2xsess||01-25-2001||08:45 PM||||I swapped in the 86GT 120mph speedo then I did the White face/blue numbers gauges faces, I agree with Ferg, getting the needles back in the right position is the biggest pain in the a$$. There are some pictures on my website. link in sig. <P>Getting the gauges out isn't real hard at all. you have to take the whole pod off. remove the back cover, there's 7 T-15/7mm screws holing it on, then remove the bottom cover, 4 7mm screws, Then you have to remove the 4 10mm that hold the pod on, then unplug all the connectors. It takes a little time the first time you do it. Then you have to take the gauges out of the pod.<P>Good luck.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG">   <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||BAM-BAM||01-25-2001||10:28 PM|||| sqoach, yes they have them for the 85MPH speedo <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/anniversarygt350/wfg.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/anniversarygt350/wfg.htm</A>   Here is a pic of mine.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dashcolor.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gauges_2.jpg"> <P> The only problem with them is that they will start peeling after a while. But they are worth the $15.00 untill I do the 120MPH conversion.<P> Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||12
Z||000006||sqoach||01-26-2001||11:44 AM||||i guess those don't look too bad. especially for $15. thanks bam.||||reg||1
